/-!
# Homogeneous branches of original 15.1.28

The source-core interface proves the original Q1 image is the two-core of
the actual seed stabilizer and places its best offender in the corresponding
restricted core. The seed retains its component Sylow fixedness and movement.

Repeated-natural multiplicity and the natural-plus-dual exclusion are proved.
The exterior branch is excluded using its full source coordinates, projected
seed and concrete seed-core exclusion. Both orthogonal modules are excluded.
The family selection returns an actual natural action equivalence. The
Coordinates and Assembly modules transport it to the original subgroup and
identify the projected seed.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.1.28, printed p.1103.
-/
